# ExamAI worker configuration.
#
# Copy to examai-api/.env. Anything left unset here falls back to the MockExams
# root .env.local, which is where GEMINI_API_KEY and the Firebase service
# account already live — no key needs copying to make this work.

# --- Auth between Next.js and this worker -----------------------------------
# REQUIRED. The worker holds Admin SDK credentials and can write any paper in
# the project, and it does NOT verify Firebase user tokens — the Next.js API
# routes do that and then call here with this key. So this value is equivalent
# to admin access: keep the worker on localhost or an internal network, and
# never expose it publicly on the strength of this key alone.
#
# The same value must be set as EXAMAI_INTERNAL_API_KEY in the root .env.local.
# Generate one with:  openssl rand -hex 32
EXAMAI_INTERNAL_API_KEY=

# --- Models -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Three roles, because the stages have genuinely different needs. Paying
# strong-model prices for OCR across a whole corpus buys nothing.

# Vision, cheap. Reading scanned pages: high volume, low reasoning.
MODEL_OCR_PROVIDER=gemini
MODEL_OCR=gemini-2.5-flash

# Strong. Writing solutions a student will memorise — the one place quality is
# worth paying for.
MODEL_SOLVE_PROVIDER=gemini
MODEL_SOLVE=gemini-2.5-pro

# Cheap. Tagging, classification, variant generation.
MODEL_CHEAP_PROVIDER=gemini
MODEL_CHEAP=gemini-2.5-flash

# --- Provider keys ----------------------------------------------------------
# Only the providers you actually select above need a key. DeepSeek has no
# vision and can never be MODEL_OCR_PROVIDER; the adapter refuses that
# combination outright rather than failing confusingly later.
GEMINI_API_KEY=
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=

# --- Postgres (the knowledge spine) -----------------------------------------
# The Supreme AI database, where the syllabus tree lives — and where documents,
# questions and solutions move as the blueprint's phases land. Start it with:
#   cd C:/SUPREME-AI && docker compose -f docker-compose.postgres.yml up -d
#
# Defaults to the DSN that compose file provisions, so local dev needs nothing
# set. Requires the ltree extension; migrations/001 creates it.
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:postgres@localhost:5432/supreme_media

# --- Firebase ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Either point at a service-account JSON:
# GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS=../serviceAccountKey.json
#
# ...or set the three variables the Node side already uses. The private key may
# contain literal \n sequences; they are normalised on load.
# FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=
# FIREBASE_CLIENT_EMAIL=
# FIREBASE_PRIVATE_KEY=

# Bucket the paper scans live in. Defaults to <project-id>.appspot.com.
# FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=

# --- Tuning -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Questions of one paper in flight at once. Small on purpose: a burst of
# concurrent calls buys little wall-clock time and makes rate limits likelier.
# EXAMAI_STAGE_CONCURRENCY=4

# Whole papers with sub-parts overflow 4096 output tokens, and a truncated
# reply arrives as unparseable JSON — which reads like a model failure rather
# than a limit. Generous by default.
# EXAMAI_EXTRACT_MAX_TOKENS=16000

# USD per million tokens, for the cost shown on the admin screen. Approximate
# and overridable: published prices change, and a stale constant silently
# understates the bill.
# EXAMAI_PRICE_IN=0.30
# EXAMAI_PRICE_OUT=2.50

# Where prompts and the generated syllabus vocabulary are read from. Defaults
# to the repo's /prompts and examai-ingest/schema.
# EXAMAI_PROMPTS_DIR=
# EXAMAI_SCHEMA_DIR=
